  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative sentiment (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00) and true prices show strong downward momentum.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp price spikes by applying a 1-2 day lag correction, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction if model consistently overpredicts prices in the 30-day horizon when recent history shows declining trends.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is neutral or slightly negative, to avoid overconfidence in upward momentum.",
    "When sentiment history includes a 0.33 or higher positive sentiment, slightly increase forecast baseline but cap at 10% above recent 15-day average to avoid overcorrection.",
    "For horizon-specific errors, reduce forecast volatility in the 30-day window if true prices show erratic or downward corrections after spikes."
  ]
}
